    "https://www.etown.edu/admissions/accepted.aspx": {
      "title": "Welcome Accepted Students",
      "description": "Accepted Students | Elizabethtown College Skip To Main Content Skip To Footer Request Information Visit Apply Deposit Give Menu Close Find Information For: Current Students Prospective Students Admitted Students Transfer Students Graduate Students Adult Learners International Students Veteran Students Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Careers at Etown Current Students Prospective Students Admitted Students Transfer Students Graduate Students Adult Learners International Students Veteran Students Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Elizabethtown College has launched a $40 million campaign to support scholarships and empower student success. Learn More Meet Etown About History Traditions Outcomes Rankings & Distinctions Office of The President President's Report Media Resources Admissions & Aid Admissions Home Apply to Etown Visit Options Request Information Transfer to Etown Tuition & Aid Financing Your Education Scholarships & Grants Meet Our Admissions Counselors Four-Year Graduation Guarantee Academics Majors & Minors Schools Online Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs School of Graduate and Professional Studies For Current Students Athletics & Life at Etown Athletics Campus Life Dining Residence Life Student Health Counseling Services Office of Student Opportunity, Access and Engagement Sustainability Support Etown Make a Gift Build Brighter Futures Institutional Advancement Volunteering Alumni Additional Resources News Events College Store Campus Map & Directory The High Library Presidential Search Bowers Center Strategic Partnerships & Innovation Employee Directory Lecture Series This site uses cookies and other tracking data to enhance user experience, analyze site traffic, and serve targeted advertisements. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy . I Understand Home Admissions accepted-students Menu Admissions Home Accepted Students Apply to Elizabethtown College Apply as a First-Year Student Apply as a Transfer Student Apply as a Homeschooled Student Apply as an International Student Incoming Class Profile Veteran Students Tuition & Costs Financial Aid & Scholarships Meet Your Counselor Find Your Major Visit Us Dual Enrollment Honors Program Four-Year Graduation Guarantee Close Menu Welcome Accepted Students Hey there, future Blue Jay! Congratulations to you on your acceptance to Etown. What’s your next step? Submit your enrollment deposit to hold your spot in the Class of 2030! Make your deposit today! You Made a Difference Elizabethtown College is thrilled to have exceeded our Make A Deposit, Make A Difference campaign for the seventh consecutive year! The campaign’s success has led to the College matching a total of $10,000 in deposits between Jan. 5 and the College’s final Accepted Student Day of the spring semester on April 18, to donate to Susquehanna Service Dogs (SSD) — an organization that trains assistance and hearing dogs to support children and adults with disabilities. Choose How to Deposit Online Log in to your Status Portal to submit your deposit! Log in now or By Mail Mail your check or money order (payable to Elizabethtown College) to: Office of Admissions Elizabethtown College 1 Alpha Drive Elizabethtown PA, 17022 After You Deposit...Celebrate! Make New Friends Introduce yourself in the Elizabethtown College Class of 2030 Accepted Students private Facebook group. Tag #etownaccepted with your new swag. Follow #bluejaysalways to connect with current and past Jays. Show off your excitement on TikTok and share the news about your acceptance to Etown with the hashtag #etownaccepted . Spread the Word Let your friends and family know you’re Etown bound! Here are some images to share on your Instagram and Snapchat accounts: Download Download Download Check Out Some of Our Visit Opportunities We offer a variety of visit options — select the one that best fits your schedule and interests. Or, view all of our visit options . Campus Visits Campus Visits include a campus tour led by a Blue Jay Ambassador and the opportunity to meet with an Admissions Counselor. Saturday Info Sessions Saturday Info Sessions are ideal for those ready to explore programs, gain insights into the application process and find out more about available scholarships. Evenings at Etown Evenings at Etown offer a convenient opportunity to fit any schedule, allowing you to discover the academic and extracurricular possibilities that await all prospective Blue Jays. Transfer Visit Days Transfer Visit Days offer tailored tours and meetings with faculty and coordinators for transfer students, focusing on exploring majors, credit transfer, and financial aid opportunities. Observe a Class Class observations allow applied students to gain firsthand insight into academic offerings and get a sense of what it's like to be a student at Etown. On-Campus Open Houses Explore all Elizabethtown College has to offer during an on-campus Open House! Tour our campus, meet our community, and discover why Etown graduates are job-ready as soon as they graduate. Contact Admissions: 717-361-1400 admissions@etown.edu More than 80% of our students live on-campus 80+ clubs and organizations “I enjoy the close-knit community at Etown. You really get to know your professors on a personal level, which makes learning more meaningful for students.” ALLISON AMSBAUGH ’23 EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION 99% of our graduates had at least one faculty member who made them excited about learning Ready to Become a Blue Jay? Deposit Now Contact Etown 717-361-1000 1 Alpha Drive Elizabethtown, PA 17022 © 2025 Elizabethtown College Additional Resources Employment Accessibility Civil Rights & Title IX Privacy Blue Jay Athletics College Store The High Library News Campus Map & Directory Campus Safety Employment Accessibility Civil Rights & Title IX Blue Jay Athletics The College Store The High Library News Campus Map & Directory Public Safety Student Health Elizabethtown College"
